Fixes #12667
Clause-②: no

The `audit:log` browser (Setup, Audit Log) offers the list views the platform serves on `sys_audit_log` as presets, and links to the object list. This is the objectui half of objectstack-ai/objectstack#23890, item 1 of objectstack-ai/objectstack#23803: "the record list's views (Writes, Auth, …) become the browser's presets; the `sys_audit_log` list stays reachable from the browser's "Open as list" link". Removing `nav_audit_logs` stays with objectstack-ai/objectstack#23890.

## What changes

- **Presets, read from served metadata.** `AuditLogPage` reads `sys_audit_log`'s `listViews` from the console's object metadata (`useMetadata().objects`, the same composed read the object list's view switcher draws from). It offers one preset per entry, by its served label, in served order. The page names no view: the test fixture uses view keys no code knows. The presets row is a group named by its visible "Presets" caption (`aria-labelledby`), not a literal `aria-label`.
- **A preset sends the view's own filter.** The view's `filter` (a spec `ViewFilterRule` array, measured live) is lowered by `@object-ui/core`'s `toFilterNodeSafely`, the same lowering the object list runs on the same view. It joins the bar's action, object, actor and date filters under one `and` via `mergeFilterNodes`. Choosing the preset again, or "Clear filters", removes it. Columns, sort and page size stay the browser's own.
- **Never approximated.** A view whose filter the lowering refuses, or one bound to another data source, is shown disabled with its reason on hover and a link to that view in the list. It sends no filter.
- **Open as list.** The header links to `/apps/APP/sys_audit_log`, or to `/apps/APP/sys_audit_log/view/KEY` when a preset is active. KEY is the `listViews` key, the same id the list's view tabs use.
- Copy stays English literals, as the rest of the page's copy is. No language-pack key, export or prop is added, so Clause-② stays `no`.

## Evidence

- Live, against `@objectstack/*@18.0.0-next.2` (showcase, `e2e/live/ci/start-backend.sh`), console at `5838608`, 1280 px:
  - the served views are `recent`, `writes_only`, `auth_events`, `record_views`, `config_changes`, `all_events`, and the presets read Recent, Writes, Auth, Record Views, Config, All;
  - Auth sends `[["action","in",["login","logout"]]]` and lists only login rows;
  - Writes lists 32 rows, and "Open as list" lands on `sys_audit_log/view/writes_only`, which lists the same 32 records;
  - the merged wire shape (bar filters plus a preset) answers HTTP 200.
  - Screenshots: branch `claude/issue-12667-evidence`, `evidence/12667/` (commit `694c35846f`).
- Tests: `AuditLogPage.presets-12667.test.tsx`, 8 tests, each family proven red by ablation:
  - views replaced by a literal list: 5 failed;
  - preset filter not sent: 2 failed;
  - Open-as-list link broken: 2 failed;
  - refused view approximated: 1 failed;
  - group named by a literal aria-label: the census and the pin both failed.
  - Every ablation was restored to the HEAD blob `a835329adbb9` with `git diff HEAD` empty.
- Three existing tests that render the page are wrapped in a `MemoryRouter`, because the page now renders a router `Link`.
- Local gates at `5838608`:
  - console dependency build, `type-check` and `vite build`;
  - vitest over `apps/console/src/pages/system` plus every console and `scripts/__tests__` file that names the page: 35 files, 271 tests passed;
  - `check:changeset-claims`, `changeset:check`, `check:test-path-roots`, `check:spec-symbols`, changeset presence, `check:new-line-citations`;
  - eslint on the changed files: no new warnings;
  - at `1e66fe2`, `packages/i18n/src/__tests__` (aria-label census included) with round 0's families: 118 files, 1593 passed.

## Acceptance notes

- The active preset is component state, like the page's other filters. Moving the filter bar into URL params under AGENTS.md #8 would be a whole-page follow-up, not this card.

